Stateless v/s Stateful - 

No data is retained , if the pod restarts / replaced nothing  imp is lost. All state is either stored in DB or doesn’t matter  at all 
Every pod is identical and replaceable  
It persist data across restarts .  We can predict the pod name and network identity . Pod name starts from 0 to N-1 pod are created  in ordinal index form. 

Stateful Applications
Definition: A stateful app stores data and depends on that data or a stable identity.
Key characteristics:
* Requires persistent storage
* Each pod has a unique identity
* Order of startup/shutdown may matter
* Data must survive pod restarts

Stateful Sets in Kubernetes -
Deployment / Replica Set are mostly for stateless Application for what we don't need to preserve the state
 
Stateful Set - for stateful application , we need dedicated  DB , persistent Storage so that if there is crash data remains intact
 
 
deployment - We dont have control over pods names controlled  by deployment , In short  network identity & Pod name cannot be predicted in advance
